# Response headers. Read natively by both Netlify and Cloudflare Pages,
# which share this file format.
#
# Only exact paths and TRAILING splats are used. Netlify's header parser
# accepts those two forms and rejects a splat in the middle of a pattern,
# so "/*.html" — which Cloudflare is happy with — fails there. The
# narrower syntax is the portable one.

# Site-wide security headers.
#
# Deliberately no Cache-Control here. Both Netlify and Cloudflare already
# serve HTML as must-revalidate by default, so setting it would be
# redundant — and setting it on /* would mean the immutable image rules
# below only work if each platform resolves overlapping rules the same
# way. Scoping cache policy to the paths that actually need it removes
# that dependency entirely.
#
# ── ON THE CSP BELOW ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# It is one line because this file has no continuation syntax: a wrapped
# value is read as a new header name and silently dropped.
#
# `script-src` carries 'unsafe-inline', and that is a real weakening
# rather than an oversight. Three kinds of inline script are load-bearing
# here: the blocking mode script that sets data-mode before first paint,
# the gtag config, and the per-page scripts. Hashes are the alternative,
# and they would break the moment a page is hand-edited — which is how
# this site is maintained. Nonces need a server that renders; this is
# static files on a CDN.
#
# So the CSP is not an XSS cure here. What it does buy, and the reason
# it is worth having:
#   - no script can load from an origin that is not listed, so injected
#     markup cannot pull in a remote payload;
#   - `connect-src` and `img-src` are narrow, so a script that did run
#     could not beacon the contact form's contents to an arbitrary host;
#   - `base-uri` stops a <base> tag rewriting every relative URL on the
#     page;
#   - `object-src`/`frame-src 'none'` remove plugin and frame vectors
#     outright.
#
# The allowed third parties are exactly the two the site actually uses:
# Google Fonts (stylesheet + font files) and Google Analytics. Adding a
# fourth means adding it here, and that is deliberate friction.
#
# ── HSTS WITHOUT preload ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# `preload` is left off on purpose. Submitting a domain to the browser
# preload list is close to irreversible — removal takes months and ships
# with the next browser release, not the next deploy — and it would apply
# to every present and future subdomain of sherjeelhussain.com. max-age
# on its own is reversible: serve a smaller value and returning browsers
# take it. Add preload only as a deliberate, separate decision.
#
# Comments live above this block rather than inside it: the two hosts
# document `#` at the start of a line, and a comment between header
# lines is not a form either of them promises to parse.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com; connect-src 'self' https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; object-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' mailto:; frame-ancestors 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Images are content-addressed in practice — a changed image gets a new
# filename — so they can be cached hard and never revalidated.
/imgs-craft/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/imgs-digital/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/imgs-expo/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/imgs-archival/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/imgs-lab/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Shared CSS/JS and the 3D scene assets change under a stable name, so
# they are cached for a day and revalidated rather than frozen for a year.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate
